{"actor":"agent:orchestrator","data":{"field":"description","from":null,"to":"Follow-up migration owed to commit 222a7fe (venue map T1/T3), raised by MRQ-4's delegator at merge.\n\n**The gap:** 222a7fe makes building geography binding for travel-conflict detection \u2014 the agenda must be able to say \"these two sessions are in different buildings N minutes apart, so this is a conflict.\" But `buildings` as shipped in MRQ-2's `0001_init.sql` has only `event_id`, `name`, `address`, `position`. There is no `lat`, no `lng`, and no `access_minutes`.\n\nMRQ-2 is merged and its migration is immutable, so this is a **second migration** (`0002_*.sql`), not an edit to the first. That is the correct outcome \u2014 M-02's \"whole schema in one migration\" guarantee covered the schema as specified at the time; this is new scope arriving after it, not a defect in it.\n\nScope:\n- `0002_venue_geography.sql`: add `buildings.lat REAL`, `buildings.lng REAL`, `buildings.access_minutes INTEGER` (walking/transit minutes between buildings, or a join table if the travel model is pairwise \u2014 read 222a7fe before choosing).\n- Mirror the columns in `src/db/schema.ts`.\n- Seed the three SPEC \u00a76 buildings with real coordinates (Sheraton New York Times Square, the Workshop Annex at the same address, Online as null/virtual).\n- Wire whatever the travel-conflict detector needs to read.\n\nDependencies: MRQ-2 (merged). Coordinate with whichever ticket owns agenda conflict detection so the reader and writer land together. Hours: ~2. Workflow: inline-full."},"id":"ev_01KZQ4RFYHCMBF9ZT08NVMNGQY","provenance":{"reason":"Schema gap from 222a7fe"},"schema_version":1,"task_id":"task_01KZQ4R4DC31HN6MERPJ0P20KP","ts":"2026-08-11T00:50:02Z","type":"field_updated"}
